      "message": {
        "content": "## 1. Insiemi, parametri e variabili decisionali\n\n### Insiemi\n\n- Centri candidati:\n\\[\nI=\\{A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H\\}\n\\]\n\n- Zone da coprire:\n\\[\nZ=\\{Z1,Z2,\\ldots,Z10\\}\n\\]\n\n- Insieme dei centri che possono coprire ciascuna zona:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nC_{Z1}&=\\{A,C\\}, & C_{Z2}&=\\{A,B\\},\\\\\nC_{Z3}&=\\{A,B,D\\}, & C_{Z4}&=\\{B,E\\},\\\\\nC_{Z5}&=\\{B,C,F\\}, & C_{Z6}&=\\{C,D,G\\},\\\\\nC_{Z7}&=\\{D,E,H\\}, & C_{Z8}&=\\{E,F,H\\},\\\\\nC_{Z9}&=\\{F,G\\}, & C_{Z10}&=\\{G,H\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\n### Parametri\n\n- Costi di apertura:\n\\[\n(c_A,c_B,c_C,c_D,c_E,c_F,c_G,c_H)\n=(24,20,27,22,25,19,23,21)\n\\]\n\n- Copertura richiesta:\n\\[\nr_z=\n\\begin{cases}\n2 & z\\in\\{Z3,Z7\\},\\\\\n1 & \\text{altrimenti}.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\n- Numero massimo di centri:\n\\[\nK=5.\n\\]\n\n### Variabili decisionali\n\nPer ogni \\(i\\in I\\):\n\\[\nx_i=\n\\begin{cases}\n1 & \\text{se il centro }i\\text{ viene aperto},\\\\\n0 & \\text{altrimenti}.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n## 2. Formulazione matematica completa\n\n### Funzione obiettivo\n\n\\[\n\\min\\quad\n24x_A+20x_B+27x_C+22x_D+25x_E+19x_F+23x_G+21x_H\n\\]\n\n### Vincoli di copertura\n\n\\[\nx_A+x_C\\geq 1 \\qquad [Z1]\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_A+x_B\\geq 1 \\qquad [Z2]\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_A+x_B+x_D\\geq 2 \\qquad [Z3]\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_B+x_E\\geq 1 \\qquad [Z4]\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_B+x_C+x_F\\geq 1 \\qquad [Z5]\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_C+x_D+x_G\\geq 1 \\qquad [Z6]\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_D+x_E+x_H\\geq 2 \\qquad [Z7]\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_E+x_F+x_H\\geq 1 \\qquad [Z8]\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_F+x_G\\geq 1 \\qquad [Z9]\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_G+x_H\\geq 1 \\qquad [Z10]\n\\]\n\n### Limite sul numero di centri\n\n\\[\nx_A+x_B+x_C+x_D+x_E+x_F+x_G+x_H\\leq 5\n\\]\n\n### Dominio\n\n\\[\nx_i\\in\\{0,1\\}\\qquad \\forall i\\in I.\n\\]\n\n---\n\n## 3. Codice Python con Gurobi\n\n```python\nimport gurobipy as gp\nfrom gurobipy import GRB\nimport json\n\ncenters = [\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\", \"E\", \"F\", \"G\", \"H\"]\nzones = [\"Z1\", \"Z2\", \"Z3\", \"Z4\", \"Z5\", \"Z6\", \"Z7\", \"Z8\", \"Z9\", \"Z10\"]\n\ncost = {\n    \"A\": 24, \"B\": 20, \"C\": 27, \"D\": 22,\n    \"E\": 25, \"F\": 19, \"G\": 23, \"H\": 21\n}\n\ncovered_zones = {\n    \"A\": {\"Z1\", \"Z2\", \"Z3\"},\n    \"B\": {\"Z2\", \"Z3\", \"Z4\", \"Z5\"},\n    \"C\": {\"Z1\", \"Z5\", \"Z6\"},\n    \"D\": {\"Z3\", \"Z6\", \"Z7\"},\n    \"E\": {\"Z4\", \"Z7\", \"Z8\"},\n    \"F\": {\"Z5\", \"Z8\", \"Z9\"},\n    \"G\": {\"Z6\", \"Z9\", \"Z10\"},\n    \"H\": {\"Z7\", \"Z8\", \"Z10\"}\n}\n\nrequired_coverage = {\n    z: (2 if z in {\"Z3\", \"Z7\"} else 1)\n    for z in zones\n}\n\nstatus_names = {\n    1: \"LOADED\",\n    2: \"OPTIMAL\",\n    3: \"INFEASIBLE\",\n    4: \"INF_OR_UNBD\",\n    5: \"UNBOUNDED\",\n    6: \"CUTOFF\",\n    7: \"ITERATION_LIMIT\",\n    8: \"NODE_LIMIT\",\n    9: \"TIME_LIMIT\",\n    10: \"SOLUTION_LIMIT\",\n    11: \"INTERRUPTED\",\n    12: \"NUMERIC\",\n    13: \"SUBOPTIMAL\",\n    14: \"INPROGRESS\",\n    15: \"USER_OBJ_LIMIT\",\n    16: \"WORK_LIMIT\",\n    17: \"MEM_LIMIT\"\n}\n\nwith gp.Env(empty=True) as env:\n    env.setParam(\"OutputFlag\", 0)\n    env.start()\n\n    with gp.Model(\"copertura_zone\", env=env) as model:\n        x = {\n            i: model.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f\"x_{i}\")\n            for i in centers\n        }\n\n        model.setObjective(\n            gp.quicksum(cost[i] * x[i] for i in centers),\n            GRB.MINIMIZE\n        )\n\n        for z in zones:\n            model.addConstr(\n                gp.quicksum(\n                    x[i] for i in centers if z in covered_zones[i]\n                ) >= required_coverage[z],\n                name=f\"copertura_{z}\"\n            )\n\n        model.addConstr(\n            gp.quicksum(x[i] for i in centers) <= 5,\n            name=\"massimo_centri\"\n        )\n\n        model.optimize()\n\n        status_code = model.Status\n        status = status_names.get(status_code, f\"STATUS_{status_code}\")\n\n        if status_code == GRB.OPTIMAL:\n            objective = float(round(model.ObjVal, 10))\n            variables = {\n                f\"x_{i}\": float(round(x[i].X))\n                for i in centers\n            }\n        else:\n            objective = None\n            variables = {}\n\n        result = {\n            \"status\": status,\n            \"objective\": objective,\n            \"variables\": variables\n        }\n\nprint(\"SOLUTION_JSON=\" + json.dumps(result, separators=(\",\", \":\")))\n```\n\n## 4. Sintesi della soluzione\n\nLo stato è **OPTIMAL** e il costo minimo è:\n\n\\[\nz^*=106.\n\\]\n\nVengono aperti i centri:\n\n\\[\nx_A=x_B=x_D=x_F=x_H=1,\n\\]\n\nmentre \\(x_C=x_E=x_G=0\\). Sono quindi aperti esattamente cinque centri. La zona \\(Z3\\) è coperta da \\(A,B,D\\), mentre \\(Z7\\) è coperta da \\(D,H\\); tutte le altre zone hanno almeno una copertura.",
